  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 28,
    "summary": "Wealth comes out of the earth—Wisdom cannot be purchased—The fear of the Lord is wisdom, and to depart from evil is understanding.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Surely there is a vein for the silver, and a place for gold where they fine it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "OR mine."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 65
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 79
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Iron is taken out of the earth, and brass is molten out of the stone.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "He setteth an end to darkness, and searcheth out all perfection: the stones of darkness, and the shadow of death.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "The flood breaketh out from the inhabitant; even the waters forgotten of the foot: they are dried up, they are gone away from men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "As for the earth, out of it cometh bread: and under it is turned up as it were fire.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "The stones of it are the place of sapphires: and it hath dust of gold.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a path which no fowl knoweth, and which the vulture’s eye hath not seen:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "The lion’s whelps have not trodden it, nor the fierce lion passed by it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "He putteth forth his hand upon the rock; he overturneth the mountains by the roots.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "He cutteth out rivers among the rocks; and his eye seeth every precious thing.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "He bindeth the floods from overflowing; and the thing that is hid bringeth he forth to light.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2,
            "text": "HEB He restricts the rivers and streams."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "But where shall wisdom be found? and where is the place of understanding?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG God, Wisdom of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG God, Wisdom of.",
            "prettyString": "TG God, Wisdom of",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "God, Wisdom of",
                "entryId": "tg-god-wisdom-of",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Man knoweth not the price thereof; neither is it found in the land of the living.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "The depth saith, It is not in me: and the sea saith, It is not with me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 22
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "It cannot be gotten for gold, neither shall silver be weighed for the price thereof.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "It cannot be valued with the gold of Ophir, with the precious onyx, or the sapphire.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "Isa. 13:12."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 9:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Isa. 13:12.",
            "prettyString": "Isaiah 13:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "isaiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 13,
                    "end": 13,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "1 Kgs. 9:28.",
            "prettyString": "1 Kings 9:28",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 28,
                        "end": 28
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "The gold and the crystal cannot equal it: and the exchange of it shall not be for jewels of fine gold.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 81
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "No mention shall be made of coral, or of pearls: for the price of wisdom is above rubies.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "Prov. 8:11 (10–11); 20:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "The topaz of Ethiopia shall not equal it, neither shall it be valued with pure gold.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Whence then cometh wisdom? and where is the place of understanding?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Seeing it is hid from the eyes of all living, and kept close from the fowls of the air.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Destruction and death say, We have heard the fame thereof with our ears.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "God understandeth the way thereof, and he knoweth the place thereof.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "For he looketh to the ends of the earth, and seeth under the whole heaven;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "To make the weight for the winds; and he weigheth the waters by measure.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "When he made a decree for the rain, and a way for the lightning of the thunder:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Then did he see it, and declare it; he prepared it, yea, and searched it out.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 28:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
